course: dictionary
lesson: 9134
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 2
explain: The word snake can mean different things. The clues around it show which meaning the writer chose. «The path snaked up the hill» uses snake as a verb: the path went in long, winding bends. The word here is an action, not an animal.
explain: Snake can also be a noun, a thing or creature. In «Snakes smell with their forked tongue», snakes are the animals. In «Don't trust Tom, he's a snake», the word is an insult: it means a person who cannot be trusted. Ask yourself what the sentence is about before you pick a meaning.
explain: Use the context check: swap your meaning into the sentence. If «The path went up the hill» still makes sense, then snaked means went in winding bends. If your meaning spoils the sentence, try another one.
fact: Snake can be a noun, meaning a reptile, or a verb, meaning to move in long bends.
fact: A snake is a reptile with no legs, and it moves by sliding along the ground.
fact: Some snakes have a venomous bite, which means their bite can poison you.
fact: «Snake» can also be an insult for a person who cannot be trusted.
fact: Snakes smell with their forked tongue, which carries scent to a special organ in the roof of the mouth.
fact: If you meet a snake, leave it alone, stand still or back away slowly, and tell an adult.
exercise: «The path snaked up the hill, round and round the rocks.» What does snaked mean here? | *Went in long, winding bends | Bit someone | Was very steep | Slid out of a hole
exercise: «Owls, foxes, cats, weasels, snakes and hawks all hunt mice.» Which animal in this list has no legs? | Hawks | Foxes | *Snakes | Owls
exercise: Tom says, «Don't trust Ella, she's a snake.» What does snake mean here? | *A person who cannot be trusted | A winding path | A board game | A long reptile with scales
test: «Some snakes have a venomous bite.» What does venomous mean? | *Able to poison with a bite | Good at swimming | Very long | Very friendly
test: «Snakes smell with their forked tongue.» Which part of a snake smells? | Its nose | *Its forked tongue | Its ears | Its tail
exam: You meet a snake in long grass. What is the safest thing to do? | Poke it with a stick | Pick it up to take a closer look | *Stand still or back away slowly, then tell an adult | Run straight towards it
